---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { repository, library } from '../lib/library';
const articles = await library();
---
<Base title="About the library" description="How Agentic Bible sources and reviews its working drafts, what those checks establish, and where editorial certification remains pending." active="about"><header class="page-intro"><p class="eyebrow">A living reference</p><h1>Clarity over hype.</h1><p>Agentic Bible is a growing encyclopedia of AI agents and the technology around them. The goal is useful context, with a visible trail back to the evidence.</p></header><div class="about-grid"><section class="prose" id="editorial"><h2>Start with the source</h2><p>Entries connect explanations to primary documentation and research. We distinguish documented behavior, illustrative examples, and project proposals. Protocol and API details change; version context and source-check dates help you judge what still applies.</p><h2>A small, honest beginning</h2><p>This edition contains {articles.length} AI-assisted working drafts. The twenty entries received deep reading across external and internal review, while factual claim verification was sampled. That work does not certify every claim or amount to human editorial certification. Each article shows its source-check date separately from its latest Git-recorded source change; when that history is unavailable, the date is shown as unknown.</p><h2>What review means here</h2><p>A source check records that cited material was consulted. It does not mean every claim was independently confirmed. Prior technical or source review of a project change is separate from a human editor certifying an article. Human editorial review remains pending unless a specific article displays an actual review record. The timing and cadence of future review are undecided.</p><p>The founder approved automatic article publication with flags for later human admin review. The public site provides reading, topic navigation, and search in your browser. Automated maintenance and public submissions are not enabled. Source evidence, technical validation, cost limits, and reversible history remain required. A separate authenticated staging workspace supports private editorial review and saved notes. Its trial does not publish changes to this public edition.</p><h2>Contributions will come later</h2><p>Public submissions are on hold while code and content licensing, contributor terms, privacy rules, and moderation are resolved. Please do not submit third-party text, code, or datasets yet.</p><a class="text-link" href={`${repository}/blob/${'feat/reference-library-slice'}/GOVERNANCE.md`}>Read the governance proposal <svg class="icon-arrow" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 13 13 3M3 3h10v10" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" /></svg></a></section><aside class="about-note"><p class="eyebrow">This edition</p><dl><div><dt>Collection</dt><dd>{articles.length} working drafts</dd></div><div><dt>Sources</dt><dd>Primary documentation & research</dd></div><div><dt>Search</dt><dd>Local, in your browser</dd></div><div><dt>Analytics & advertising</dt><dd>Disabled</dd></div></dl><p>No accounts, tracking scripts, or AI requests are needed to read or search. Search terms stay in the browser’s URL fragment; this app does not send them to a search service.</p></aside></div></Base>
